[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports describe
two different bugs. The queued fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket now. Close #4471 only when both
are fixed.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day
  first, so day and month swap. This is the fix that #4471 queued.
- **`hint`**: the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what
  the hint says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does
  not touch the form.

## How the reports were sorted

- One id, one report. The export has repeated rows from overlapping pages.
- The tenant decides the cause: its locale and its booking form (`causes.ts`). The intake tag
  is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it is wrong for many of these reports.
- Subject lines do not separate the problems. The same subjects appear under both.
- Reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) stay with their tenant's cause.

